;; The Lonely Rover's opening (issue #61): the storm has weakened a section of the crater's rim
;; (racket/maps/victoria.rkt), and the world begins with it coming down, on screen, onto the
;; cargo that stands at its foot. Five crates up the slope from the cliff, along its middle
;; (azimuth 30); which the rubble buries, and under how much, is where the ground's physics
;; puts it, the same each run. The rim is rocky: 2% of what comes down comes down as 2 m
;; cubes of granite, 21.6 t each, which roll down the rubble and stop on it. Where the cargo
;; stands is the scenario's choice (#60): the battery bank's place was picked so that one of
;; them comes to rest on the rubble over it, and a backhoe that can't lift a boulder has to
;; get it off the bank some other way.
(world lonely-rover-opening
  ;; the scenario (#60): what this world is for, as the front end lists it. No tuning: every number is the real one.
  (scenario
    (title "The Lonely Rover")
    (description "Mars, a crater, a storm that has brought a weakened rim down on your cargo. Dig out the battery bank, make electricity without panels, keep the bank warm through the night, and call Earth on the pre-dawn relay pass. The real numbers.")
    (tuning (bank-capacity 0.1)))
  (map victoria)
  ;; the player's rover (#94): 45 m down the slope from the first crate, facing it (+x), where the floor is only ~7 degrees
  (rover (at 190.0 140.0) (heading 270))
  (place battery-bank found-bank (at 264.0 0 143.0))
  (place solar-panels cargo-crate (at 254.62 0 147.0))
  (place gas-cylinders cargo-crate (at 249.42 0 144.0))
  (place hand-tools cargo-crate (at 242.49 0 140.0))
  (place spares cargo-crate (at 233.83 0 135.0)))
